Reverts the PPU drawing optimizations, to compare them against the current core.

Turns the drawing loops back into their original form: the tile row address and
its two bytes are recomputed for every pixel, VRAM and OAM are reached through
the memory bus instead of being indexed directly, the sprite to background
priority is resolved by reading the framebuffer back instead of using a cache,
and the tile coordinates use divisions instead of shifts. It also marks every
draw_ function as #[inline(never)], so that each one shows up as its own frame
in a flamegraph.

    git apply core/examples/ppu_profile/ppu_profile.patch
    just flamegraph-core --freq 499 -- <rom> 40000
    git apply -R core/examples/ppu_profile/ppu_profile.patch

To profile the current version under the same conditions, apply only the
#[inline(never)] hunks of core/src/ppu/mod.rs below. Without them LLVM inlines
draw_bg into Ppu::step and the drawing does not appear as a separate frame.

Sampling above ~500 Hz drops chunks on this workload and the PPU disappears
from the graph, hence the --freq 499.

